    {
      "abstract": "This dataset includes benchmark data of a tension-leg-platform-type floating offshore wind turbine with integrated artificial reef structures (ARS) and a technical report with a brief description of the experimental campaign. The experimental campaign was carried out at the Coastal and Ocean Basin (COB) in Oostende, Belgium as part of Task 4.5 of the INF4INiTY project. The dataset includes the platform motions, accelerations at the nacelle and tensions in the mooring lines under regular, irregular and focused wave conditions, with and without currents, and for multiple ARS configurations at a 1:62.5 model scale. In addition to the dataset, the technical report includes a complete description of the scale model, the experimental set-up, the testing procedure, the instrumentation and data acquisition systems employed, and the postprocessing techniques. The aim of this dataset is two-fold. On the one hand, it provides a first characterisation of the INF4INiTY nature-inclusive design solutions and their impact on the hydrodynamic behaviour of floating platforms. On the other hand, the dataset provides researchers, technology developers and industry with benchmarking data for numerical validation of hydrodynamic models, as well as insights into how of ARS affect the floating platform response.",
